## Route Protection ##
Just check if User is logged in, proceed to route handler
    Returns 401 Unauthorized if not authenticated
    All diary routes require authentication
    In addition to authentication, each controller function enforces ownership:
    Route Level: ensureAuthenticated blocks unauthenticated requests
    Query Level: find  filters entries by owner
    Controller Level: Explicit ownership comparison for single-entry operations

## Logout Route ##
req.logout() - Passport method that:
    Removes the req.user property
    Terminates the login session
req.session.destroy() - Express-session method that:
    Deletes the session data from the server
    Prevents the session ID from being reused
res.clearCookie("connect.sid") - Removes the cookie from the client browser
Response - Returns success message to client

Before Logout:
    GET /auth/current-user
    GET /api/diary
After Logout:
    GET /auth/current-user 
    GET /api/diary

## Testing Strategies ##
http://localhost:5000/auth/google

npm run dev
Open Chrome and navigate to: http://localhost:5000/auth/google
    Redirect to Google login screen
    Select your Google account
    Click "Continue" to grant permissions
    Redirect back to success message
Chrome:
    Press F12 to open Developer Tools
    Go to Application tab
    Expand Cookies → http://localhost:5000
    Find connect.sid cookie
    Copy the entire Value
Add Cookie to Postman:
    Open Postman Desktop App
    Click "Cookies" link under the Send button
    Click "Add Domain" → Enter localhost
    Click "Add Cookie" and fill:
        Name: connect.sid
        Value: [paste from browser]
        Domain: localhost
        Path: /

